## Star Wars
// A guide to the galaxy, from two servers other people run, in one program:
//   swapi.info knows the films, people, planets and ships, and links them to each other by address
//   Wikipedia has the pictures, one page at a time
// Say what a field links to, and reading it follows the link:  `the name of its homeworld`.
// `star wars` and its types' fields are what this wrote, from looking at the server, cut down to what's used here:
//   spell place ingest https://swapi.info/api --into StarWars.spell --name "star wars"
//
// Star Wars and its pictures belong to Lucasfilm and Disney, the words to Wikipedia's writers.
// They're asked for as it runs, never kept here, and the page says where they come from.


## Where it all lives
star wars is a web server at "https://swapi.info/api":
	- its id is its "url"
	- check it every 86400 seconds
	- films live at "/films"
	- people live at "/people"
	- planets live at "/planets"
	- species live at "/species"
	- vehicles live at "/vehicles"
	- starships live at "/starships"
	- a film's episode id is its "episode_id"
	- a film's opening crawl is its "opening_crawl"
	- a film's release date is its "release_date"
	- a person's hair color is its "hair_color"
	- a person's eye color is its "eye_color"
	- a person's birth year is its "birth_year"
	- a planet's rotation period is its "rotation_period"
	- a planet's orbital period is its "orbital_period"
	- a planet's surface water is its "surface_water"
	- a species's average lifespan is its "average_lifespan"
	- a vehicle's "cost in credits" is its "cost_in_credits"
	- a vehicle's craft class is its "vehicle_class"
	- a starship's "cost in credits" is its "cost_in_credits"
	- a starship's craft class is its "starship_class"

wikipedia is a web server at "https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1":
	- check it every 86400 seconds
	- wiki pages live at "/page/summary"
	- a wiki page's id is its "pageid"
	- a wiki page's picture is its "thumbnail.source"
	- a wiki page's about is its "description"
	- a wiki page's summary is its "extract"
	- a wiki page's address is its "content_urls.desktop.page"


## The app:  what's showing, and how you get about
guide is an app:
	- its "tab" is text
	- its "search" is text
	- its "showing" is a record
	- its "trail" is a new list of records
	- its "playing" is a film
	- its "jumping" is yes or no
	- its "how many" is a number
	- its "looking for" is its search as lower case

	// What the shelf lists:  whatever's found, else its tab's, a few at a time
	- its "listed" is:
		if its search is not ""
			return its found
		if its tab is "films"
			return every film
		if its tab is "people"
			return top (its how many) items of (every person)
		if its tab is "planets"
			return top (its how many) items of (every planet)
		if its tab is "vehicles"
			return top (its how many) items of (every vehicle)
		if its tab is "species"
			return top (its how many) items of (every species)
		return top (its how many) items of (every starship)

	- its "found" is:
		set matches to a new list of records
		for each film in every film where (its title as lower case) includes the looking for of the guide
			add the film to matches
		for each person in every person where (its name as lower case) includes the looking for of the guide
			add the person to matches
		for each planet in every planet where (its name as lower case) includes the looking for of the guide
			add the planet to matches
		for each starship in every starship where (its name as lower case) includes the looking for of the guide
			add the starship to matches
		for each vehicle in every vehicle where (its name as lower case) includes the looking for of the guide
			add the vehicle to matches
		for each one in every species where (its name as lower case) includes the looking for of the guide
			add the one to matches
		return matches

	- to create it:
		set its tab to "films"
		set its how many to 12

	- to go back:
		if its trail is empty
			set its showing to nothing
			return
		set its showing to the last item of its trail
		remove the last item of its trail
		scroll to the top

	- to go to (where as text):
		set its tab to where
		set its search to ""
		set its showing to nothing
		clear its trail
		set its how many to 12
		scroll to the top

	- to show more:
		set its how many to its how many + 12

	// Punch it:  a jump to light speed, and wherever it lands
	- to punch it:
		set its jumping to yes
		set landing to a random person in (every person)
		pause for 900 msec
		open landing
		set its jumping to no

	- to draw it:
		<div class="stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
		if its jumping
			<div class="jump" aria-hidden="true"></div>
		<header class="top">
			<ui-button class="logo" appearance="transparent" onClick={go to "films"}>Star Wars</ui-button>
			<ui-form value={it} class="find">
				<ui-field label="Search the galaxy">
					<ui-input name="search" icon="search" placeholder="Luke, Hoth, Falcon"/>
				</ui-field>
			</ui-form>
			<ui-button class="punch" color="primary" onClick={punch it} title="Jump to light speed, and land on someone">Punch it</ui-button>
		</header>
		<ui-toolbar class="tabs" appearance="secondary pointing" aria-label="Browse">
			<ui-item active={its tab is "films"} onClick={go to "films"}>Films</ui-item>
			<ui-item active={its tab is "people"} onClick={go to "people"}>People</ui-item>
			<ui-item active={its tab is "planets"} onClick={go to "planets"}>Planets</ui-item>
			<ui-item active={its tab is "ships"} onClick={go to "ships"}>Ships</ui-item>
			<ui-item active={its tab is "vehicles"} onClick={go to "vehicles"}>Vehicles</ui-item>
			<ui-item active={its tab is "species"} onClick={go to "species"}>Species</ui-item>
		</ui-toolbar>
		<main class="shelf">
			{draw its shelf}
		</main>
		<footer class="credits">
			Films, people, planets and ships from <a href="https://swapi.info/">swapi.info</a>.
			Pictures and what they're of from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/">Wikipedia</a>, asked for as you look.
			Star Wars belongs to Lucasfilm and Disney.
		</footer>
		if its playing
			draw the crawl of its playing

	- to draw its shelf:
		if its showing and its search is ""
			draw the page of its showing
		otherwise
			if its search is not ""
				<h2 class="heading">Searching for “{its search}”</h2>
			for each record in its listed
				draw the record
			while waiting:
				<div class="wide"><ui-loader visible inline text>Waiting for a signal from swapi.info</ui-loader></div>
			if there are none:
				<p class="none">Nobody and nothing by that name, in this galaxy.</p>
			if that fails:
				<div class="wide">
					<ui-message color="red">
						<p>The signal from swapi.info is lost.</p>
						<ui-button onClick={try again}>Try again</ui-button>
					</ui-message>
				</div>
			draw (a new more button)


## Show more:  only for a list with more to show, so it isn't all asked of Wikipedia at once
a "more button" is a thing:
	- its "full" is (the number of items in the listed of the guide) is the how many of the guide
	- to draw it:
		<div class={"wide" if its full otherwise "hidden"}>
			<ui-button class="more" onClick={show more of the guide}>Show more</ui-button>
		</div>
		while waiting:
			<div class="hidden"></div>
		if that fails:
			<div class="hidden"></div>


## A page of Wikipedia:  not every name has one, and a name may be someone else's (Zolan is a medicine)
a "wiki page" is a thing:
	- it lives in wikipedia
	- its "title" is text
	- its "about" is text
	- its "summary" is text
	- its "picture" is text
	- its "address" is text
	- its "lower about" is its about as lower case
	- its "fits" is:
		if its title includes "List of"
			return no
		return its lower about includes "star wars" or its lower about includes "fictional" or its lower about includes " film "


## A picture:  its own page on Wikipedia, if it has one, else an initial on a colour
a "portrait" is a thing:
	- its "name" is text
	- its "hue" is a number
	- its "shape" is text
	- its "page" is the wiki page whose id is its name
	- its "initial" is the first letter of its name
	- its "picture" is:
		if its page and the fits of its page
			return the picture of its page
		return ""
	- to draw it:
		<span class={"portrait " + its shape} style={"--hue: " + its hue}>
			<span class="initial">{its initial}</span>
			{draw its photo}
		</span>
	// Waiting for it, or if Wikipedia can't be reached, the initial stays
	- to draw its photo:
		<img class={"hidden" if its picture is "" otherwise ""} src={its picture} alt=""/>
		while waiting:
			<span class="hidden"></span>
		if that fails:
			<span class="hidden"></span>


## What Wikipedia says of it, and where to read the rest
a "wiki note" is a thing:
	- its "name" is text
	- its "page" is the wiki page whose id is its name
	- to draw it:
		<p class={"note" if its page and the fits of its page otherwise "hidden"}>{the summary of its page} <a href={the address of its page} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the rest on Wikipedia</a></p>
		while waiting:
			<p class="note waiting">Asking Wikipedia</p>
		if that fails:
			<p class="note waiting">Wikipedia can't be reached just now.</p>


## What they all have:  a card to click, a picture, a page
a "record" is a thing:
	- its "label" is text
	- its "kind" is text
	- its "shape" is text
	- its "hue" is the length of its label * 47

	// A number for people to read, or that nobody knows
	- to measure (amount as a number) in (unit as text):
		if amount is nothing
			return "unknown"
		return amount with commas + " " + unit

	- to open it:
		if the showing of the guide
			add the showing of the guide to the trail of the guide
		set the search of the guide to ""
		set the showing of the guide to it
		scroll to the top

	- to draw it:
		<ui-card class="card" appearance="link">
			{draw (a new portrait with name = its label, hue = its hue, shape = its shape)}
			<div class="words">
				<ui-button class="open" appearance="transparent" onClick={open it}>{its label}</ui-button>
				<small>{its kind}</small>
			</div>
		</ui-card>

	- to draw its page:
		<div></div>

	// What a page can do besides read:  nothing, unless it says
	- to draw its actions:
		<span></span>

	- to draw its top:
		<ui-button class="back" appearance="transparent" icon="arrow left" onClick={go back}>Back</ui-button>
		<div class="hero">
			{draw (a new portrait with name = its label, hue = its hue, shape = its shape)}
			<div class="about">
				<h2>{its label}</h2>
				<p class="kind">{its kind}</p>
				{draw its actions}
				{draw (a new wiki note with name = its label)}
			</div>
		</div>


## A film
a "film" is a record:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "title" is text
	- its "episode id" is a number
	- its "opening crawl" is text
	- its "director" is text
	- its "producer" is text
	- its "release date" is a date
	- its "characters" is a list of people
	- its "planets" is a list of planets
	- its "starships" is a list of starships
	- its "label" is its title
	- its "kind" is "Episode " + its episode id

	- to play it:
		set the playing of the guide to it

	- to end it:
		set the playing of the guide to nothing

	- to draw its actions:
		<ui-button class="play" onClick={play it}>Play the opening</ui-button>

	- to draw its page:
		draw its top
		<ui-table class="facts" appearance="very-basic" unstackable><table><tbody>
			<tr><th>Directed by</th><td>{its director}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Produced by</th><td>{its producer}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Released</th><td>{its release date}</td></tr>
		</tbody></table></ui-table>
		<h3>Who's in it</h3>
		for each person in its characters
			draw the person
		while waiting:
			<ui-loader class="waiting" visible inline text>Following the links</ui-loader>
		<h3>Where it happens</h3>
		for each planet in its planets
			draw the planet
		<h3>What they fly</h3>
		for each starship in its starships
			draw the starship

	// The opening:  yellow, receding, and it stops when you say
	- to draw its crawl:
		<ui-modal class="crawl" visible overlay fullscreen on-ui-closed={end it} aria-label={"The opening of " + its title}><div class="cinema">
			<div class="stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
			<p class="long-ago">A long time ago in a galaxy far, far away....</p>
			<div class="stage">
				<div class="words">
					<p class="episode">Episode {its episode id}</p>
					<h2>{its title}</h2>
					<p class="text">{its opening crawl}</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<ui-button class="stop" onClick={end it}>Stop</ui-button>
		</div></ui-modal>


## A person
a "person" is a record:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "height" is a number
	- its "mass" is a number
	- its "hair color" is text
	- its "eye color" is text
	- its "birth year" is text
	- its "gender" is text
	- its "homeworld" is a planet
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "species" is a list of species
	- its "vehicles" is a list of vehicles
	- its "starships" is a list of starships
	- its "label" is its name
	- its "kind" is "Born " + its birth year

	- to draw its page:
		draw its top
		<ui-table class="facts" appearance="very-basic" unstackable><table><tbody>
			<tr><th>Height</th><td class="number">{measure its height in "cm"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Mass</th><td class="number">{measure its mass in "kg"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Born</th><td>{its birth year}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Hair</th><td>{its hair color}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Eyes</th><td>{its eye color}</td></tr>
		</tbody></table></ui-table>
		<h3>Home</h3>
		draw its homeworld
		<h3>Films</h3>
		for each film in its films
			draw the film
		while waiting:
			<ui-loader class="waiting" visible inline text>Following the links</ui-loader>
		<h3>What they are</h3>
		for each one in its species
			draw the one
		if there are none:
			<p class="none">Human, as far as anyone says.</p>
		<h3>What they fly</h3>
		for each starship in its starships
			draw the starship
		for each vehicle in its vehicles
			draw the vehicle


## A planet
a "planet" is a record:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "rotation period" is a number
	- its "orbital period" is a number
	- its "diameter" is a number
	- its "climate" is text
	- its "gravity" is text
	- its "terrain" is text
	- its "surface water" is a number
	- its "population" is a number
	- its "residents" is a list of people
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "label" is its name
	- its "kind" is its climate
	- its "shape" is "world"
	// what colour a world is, from its weather
	- its "hue" is:
		if its climate includes "frozen"
			return 200
		if its climate includes "arid"
			return 38
		if its climate includes "murky" or its climate includes "polluted"
			return 95
		if its climate includes "tropical" or its climate includes "temperate"
			return 130 + the length of its label * 9
		return 280

	- to draw its page:
		draw its top
		<ui-table class="facts" appearance="very-basic" unstackable><table><tbody>
			<tr><th>Climate</th><td>{its climate}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Terrain</th><td>{its terrain}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Diameter</th><td class="number">{measure its diameter in "km"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Population</th><td class="number">{measure its population in "people"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>A day</th><td class="number">{measure its rotation period in "hours"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>A year</th><td class="number">{measure its orbital period in "days"}</td></tr>
		</tbody></table></ui-table>
		<h3>Who's from here</h3>
		for each person in its residents
			draw the person
		if there are none:
			<p class="none">Nobody we know of.</p>
		<h3>Seen in</h3>
		for each film in its films
			draw the film
		if there are none:
			<p class="none">No film.</p>


## A ship, or a vehicle:  much the same to look at
a "craft" is a record:
	- its "name" is text
	- its "model" is text
	- its "manufacturer" is text
	- its "cost in credits" is a number
	- its "length" is a number
	- its "crew" is text
	- its "passengers" is a number
	- its "craft class" is text
	- its "pilots" is a list of people
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "label" is its name
	- its "kind" is its craft class
	// how long it is, in something you can picture:  an X-wing is 12.5 metres
	- its "x-wings long" is:
		if its length is nothing
			return nothing
		return round (its length / 12.5)

	- to draw its page:
		draw its top
		<ui-table class="facts" appearance="very-basic" unstackable><table><tbody>
			<tr><th>Model</th><td>{its model}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Made by</th><td>{its manufacturer}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Length</th><td class="number">{measure its length in "m"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>As long as</th><td class="number">{measure its x-wings long in "X-wings"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Crew</th><td class="number">{its crew}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Passengers</th><td class="number">{measure its passengers in "people"}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Costs</th><td class="number">{measure its cost in credits in "credits"}</td></tr>
		</tbody></table></ui-table>
		<h3>Who flew it</h3>
		for each person in its pilots
			draw the person
		if there are none:
			<p class="none">Nobody named.</p>
		<h3>Seen in</h3>
		for each film in its films
			draw the film

a "starship" is a craft:
	- it lives in star wars

a "vehicle" is a craft:
	- it lives in star wars


## A species
a "species" is a record:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "classification" is text
	- its "language" is text
	- its "average lifespan" is text
	- its "homeworld" is a planet
	- its "people" is a list of people
	- its "label" is its name
	- its "kind" is its classification

	- to draw its page:
		draw its top
		<ui-table class="facts" appearance="very-basic" unstackable><table><tbody>
			<tr><th>Language</th><td>{its language}</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Lives for</th><td>{its average lifespan}</td></tr>
		</tbody></table></ui-table>
		<h3>Home</h3>
		draw its homeworld
		<h3>Who's one</h3>
		for each person in its people
			draw the person
		if there are none:
			<p class="none">Nobody we know of.</p>
